// Talk: what agents say to each other, questions, claims and answers,
// accounts, a lie; and records, written and read (KNOWLEDGE.md §10, §15;
// AGENCY.md decision 11; KNOWLEDGE.md Scenario 1, "the rumour of the
// nails").
//
// Cut points:
// - full:      whoever is in earshot hears what is said.
// - reduced:   an agent hears only what is said to it.
// - abstract:  as reduced. News held by communities, moving along routes, is
//              planned (DETAIL_REGIMES.md).
// - frozen:    it hears nothing.
// - contact:   being spoken to by someone at full detail raises an agent to
//              full while the contact lease runs (reality.tri).
// - knowledge: the shapes of claims (#Utterance, #Telling, ...) are
//              knowledge.tri's; a topic's own claims are in its directory.
// - code:      effect_say, effect_write, effect_read; what a hearer makes of
//              what it hears is src/know_knowledge_*.odin's.

package talk

// Where is something like `what`?
#WhereIs: #Question & {}

// Someone shouts the hearer's name (`what`: the hearer, by looks): a call,
// answered with `#Here`, which may be worth putting down what it is doing
// (AGENCY.md §7, a soft interruption).
#Call: #Question & {}
#Here: #Utterance & {}

// Who told you something like `what` is inside `within`? (questioning a
// source, KNOWLEDGE.md §10). The answer is the claim again, with its source.
#WhoToldYou: #Question & #Placing & {}

// A claim: something like `what` is inside `within`.
#IsIn: #Placing & #Telling & {}

// A claim: something like `what` is like `as` (its features: "the nut is
// 22 mm"). Where it conflicts with what the hearer believes of it, the two
// coexist as competing hypotheses (KNOWLEDGE.md §11), the claim's as
// credible as the hearer finds the speaker.
#IsLike: #Telling & { as: #Body }

// A claim: something like `what` is held by someone like `holder`.
#IsHeld: #Naming & {}

// The speaker knows of nothing like `what` that it could say where it is.
#DontKnow: #Utterance & {}

// The speaker won't say where something like `what` is, or give it
// (AGENCY.md §11).
#WontSay: #Utterance & {}

// Say something to an agent in reach. What is said is the command's.
say: #Operation & {
    effect:   "say"
    duration: 1s
    uses:     ["voice"]
    roles: {
        actor: #Agent
        item:  #Agent
    }
} @family(operations)

// Records (KNOWLEDGE.md §10, §15): a body that carries writing. Writing is
// the copy operation: what the writer believes becomes content, with the
// writer as its author; whoever reads it gains claims whose source is the
// author and whose medium is the record. It can be stolen, and read by the
// thief, and the writer's memory is untouched.
#Record: #Body & {
    @component(Record)
    writing: text @field(saved, proposable, inspect)
}

record_seen: #Seen & { kindOf: "#Record" } @family(seen)

// A label (ACTIONS.md §7's tag on a shelf): a record whose writing anyone
// within `legible` tiles of it reads at a glance, on sighting it.
#Label: #Record & {
    @component(Label)
    legible: int & >=0 & <=8                @field(content, saved, inspect, perceive(sight))
}

label_seen: #Seen & { kindOf: "#Label" } @family(seen)

// Claims, in order: written, or told one after another.
#Entries: { entries: [...#Telling] }

// What a record holds: who wrote it, by their looks, and the claims written.
#Writing: #Entries & { author: #Agent }

// An account (ACTIONS.md decision 14): several claims about something like
// `what`, said together. Saying it takes a second more for each claim after
// the first; a hearer takes in each.
#Account: #Utterance & #Entries & {}

// Write a claim into a record the actor holds. What is written is the
// command's: a #Writing with one entry.
write_down: #Operation & {
    effect: "write"
    uses:   ["hands"]
    roles: {
        actor: #Agent & { id: $a }
        item:  #Record & { place: #Held & { by: $a } }
    }
} @family(operations)

// Read a record within reach: a second's reading, what it holds taken in
// when it ends.
read: #Operation & {
    effect:   "read"
    duration: 1s
    roles: {
        actor: #Agent
        item:  #Record
    }
} @family(operations)

// Escaping a consequence: the theft the truth would expose, against its
// honesty, and the risk of being found out (the thing in sight of someone).
deny_it: #Lie & {
    title: "deny it"
    score: [#Exposing & { exposing: "what", act: "#Taking" }, #Trait & { trait: "honesty", per: -5 },
            #Watched & { watched: "what", penalty: 20 }]
} @family(lies)

// For the notebook: a record a character writes in, which can be stolen.
notebook: #Record & { material: "paper", mass: 200g }

// Someone with two hands to work with.
let person = #Hungry & { material: "flesh", hands: 2 }

// For KNOWLEDGE.md's first scenario, as "the rumour of the nails": a carter
// and a porter the apprentice tells, a neighbour who saw it too, and
// the foreman who hears it from them all.
carter:    #Agent & person & { mass: 75kg, coat: "red" }
porter:    #Agent & person & { mass: 80kg, coat: "yellow" }
neighbour: #Agent & person & { mass: 60kg, coat: "grey" }
foreman:   #Agent & person & { mass: 90kg, coat: "black", painting: 50 }

// For salience and bounded stores: someone who keeps little in mind.
gossip: #Agent & person & { mass: 65kg, coat: "beige", memory: 4 }
